    2. Assign each color a unique object count from {1..5} ensuring all counts distinct.
       Sort descending to get the histogram row order.
    3. Build the output histogram grid (K rows x max_count cols).
    4. Create a 16x16 black grid. For each color, place its N squares (random sizes
       2-5) without overlapping or 8-touching any existing object. Use rejection
       sampling per placement; retry with smaller size if needed.
    5. Return the 16x16 grid as input.
